<h1>{{ project_name }}</h1>
<p>
  A small C++17 StreamPU pipeline generated by Hulotte. The graph is explicit in
  <code>src/main.cpp</code>; edit the C++ directly.
</p>
<h2>Build and run</h2>
<p>Set <code>STREAMPU_ROOT</code> to the StreamPU source tree, then run:</p>
<pre><code>cmake -S . -B build&#10;cmake --build build&#10;./build/{{ executable_name }}&#10;ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure</code></pre>
<p>
  The initial pipeline connects a random integer source to the custom
  <code>PassThrough</code> module and a <code>Comparator</code> reference path.
  It executes three frames and exits with an error if any output element differs
  from the source.
</p>
<p>
  Added custom modules live under <code>src/custom/</code>. Integrate their
  includes, instances, and socket bindings into
  <code>src/main.cpp</code> manually, replacing any existing binding to the same
  input socket. CMake discovers added <code>.cpp</code> files automatically. A
  file under <code>src/hw/</code> enables Verilator and must define a top-level
  module matching the filename.
</p>
<p>
  Hardware wrappers use equal-length 32-bit integer frames and retain their RTL
  state across frames. A simulation timeout raises an error. To collect a VCD,
  pass a distinct output path as the adapter's second constructor argument.
  Trace paths are relative to the executable's working directory.
</p>
